cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CCA, please cite it as below, together with the works it builds on (docs/science.md)."
type: software
title: "CCA (C-AIME decision core)"
abstract: >-
  A research layer over Stockfish and Maia-2 designed to play human-like, hard-to-predict,
  opponent-aware chess (these behavioural goals are pre-registered hypotheses, not measured results): closed-form piKL anchored on a human move model, human-aware
  look-ahead with safe exploitation, latent control variables inspired by (not models of)
  stress and reward-prediction-error findings, and a reproducible Lorenz-63 variability
  driver with a stochastic control condition.
authors:
